            "id": "4954785",
            "title": "Riverwater Partners Q3 2026 Small Cap Macro Letter",
            "description": "<html><body><p data-eci=\"true\"><figure class=\"getty-figure\" data-type=\"getty-image\"><picture> <img alt=\"Financial saving concept\" data-id=\"1329972605\" data-type=\"getty-image\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"1025\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 132px), (max-width: 1199px) calc(100vw - 666px), (max-width: 1307px) calc(100vw - 708px), 600px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1329972605/image_1329972605.jpg?io=getty-c-w630\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1329972605/image_1329972605.jpg?io=getty-c-w1536 1536w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1329972605/image_1329972605.jpg?io=getty-c-w1280 1280w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1329972605/image_1329972605.jpg?io=getty-c-w1080 1080w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1329972605/image_1329972605.jpg?io=getty-c-w750 750w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1329972605/image_1329972605.jpg?io=getty-c-w640 640w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1329972605/image_1329972605.jpg?io=getty-c-w480 480w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1329972605/image_1329972605.jpg?io=getty-c-w320 320w, https://static.seekingalpha.com/cdn/s3/uploads/getty_images/1329972605/image_1329972605.jpg?io=getty-c-w240 240w\" width=\"1536\"/> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"> </p> <p class=\"item-credits\">shylendrahoode/iStock via Getty Images</p></figcaption></figure></p> <h2>Small Caps, Oil &amp; the First Fed Hike</h2> <h2>Ten Years of Responsible Small-Cap Investing</h2> <p>This past spring marked a decade since Riverwater opened its doors, and we were delighted to celebrate the milestone with our valued clients and friends a few weeks ago. We have a lot to be proud of. Since the Sustainable Value strategy’s inception in 2016, it has outperformed the <a href=\"https://www.lseg.com/en/ftse-russell/indices/russell-us\" rel=\"noopener\">Russell 2500 Value Index</a> net of fees, with lower volatility as measured by standard deviation and beta, although results have varied from year to year.<sup>1</sup></p> <p>It’s enlightening to look back and reflect on how much the world has changed in just ten years. In 2016, interest rates were near zero, few adults had ever experienced a global airborne pandemic, and artificial intelligence was just beginning to move from science fiction to the real world. Most small-cap companies were not reporting on sustainability initiatives, and we often had to explain to management teams the benefits of doing so.</p> <p>Fast forward to today, and we are navigating an environment marked by elevated inflation and higher interest rates, the scars of COVID, an economy now firmly driven by AI, and widespread market appreciation for sustainable business practices.</p> <p>Our team is asking: What will the next ten years look like, and how must our approach evolve to satisfy our core mission? There is no way to see out that far, but we don’t think it’s necessary to. We have built a team, a process, and a framework that we believe can adapt to the ever-changing world and deliver results over the long term.</p> <h2>Small Caps in a Narrow, AI-Driven Market</h2> <p>Thinking long term while managing capital in the short term can be frustrating, especially in markets as narrow as today’s. Investors have become almost singularly focused on AI, energy, and companies that haven’t yet turned profitable, leaving high-quality companies in other sectors largely overlooked.</p> <p>We began building exposure to AI infrastructure, semiconductor capital equipment and optical components early in the buildout for our small-cap strategies, and those holdings were key performance drivers over the past year in those strategies. As valuations outpaced sales and cash flows, we trimmed or sold most of those positions, which pushed turnover above our historical norm. We have redeployed that capital into companies we believe offer more attractive long-term risk and reward.</p> <h2>Oil Prices, Inflation, and the Fed’s First Hike</h2> <p>Higher oil prices are both inflationary and act as a direct tax on the consumer. To curb this energy-driven inflation, the Federal Reserve raised short-term interest rates at its September meeting.<sup>2</sup> Interest rates matter for everything: inflation, stock valuations, real estate, you name it. Notably, the Fed has not begun a hiking cycle after an oil surge this large in more than four decades. This cycle stands apart: oil is up roughly 60% in the past year versus a median decline of 4% ahead of the prior seven rate-hiking cycles since 1983.<sup>3</sup></p> <p><figure class=\"regular-img-figure\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <span><a aria-label=\"Expand image into lightbox view\" data-height=\"563\" data-og-image-facebook=\"true\" data-og-image-google_news=\"true\" data-og-image-google_plus=\"true\" data-og-image-linkedin=\"true\" data-og-image-msn=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_image_post=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_large_card=\"true\" data-og-image-twitter_small_card=\"true\" data-width=\"1129\" href=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-17921577389487443_origin.png\" rel=\"lightbox\" role=\"button\"><img alt=\"WTI\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"319\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-17921577389487443_origin.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-17921577389487443_origin.png?io=w640 640w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-17921577389487443_origin.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-17921577389487443_origin.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-17921577389487443_origin.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"640\"/></a></span> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"> </p></figcaption></figure></p> <p>The key question is whether energy-driven headline inflation will seep into goods and services prices, pushing up core inflation and unanchoring long-anchored inflation expectations.</p> <p>The war in the Persian Gulf makes oil supply, and by extension inflation and the Fed’s path, genuinely unknowable. What we do know is how small-caps have fared historically in these environments.</p> <h2>How Small Caps Perform After a Fed Rate Hike</h2> <p>On average, the <a href=\"https://www.lseg.com/en/ftse-russell/indices/russell-us\" rel=\"noopener\">Russell 2000</a> has gained 4% twelve months after the first hike, with a median return of 8%. Across the seven prior cycles, the twelve-month return ranged from -13% (2022) to +19% (2015).<sup>4</sup> The future direction of near-term returns for small caps in a rate-hiking cycle is a coin flip. History tells us that small caps prefer core inflation below 2.5%, with the strongest median returns when it is also falling.</p> <p><figure class=\"regular-img-figure\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <span><a aria-label=\"Expand image into lightbox view\" data-height=\"321\" data-og-image-facebook=\"false\" data-og-image-google_news=\"false\" data-og-image-google_plus=\"false\" data-og-image-linkedin=\"false\" data-og-image-msn=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_image_post=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_large_card=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_small_card=\"false\" data-width=\"1074\" href=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-17921577917554438_origin.png\" rel=\"lightbox\" role=\"button\"><img alt=\"R2000\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"191\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-17921577917554438_origin.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-17921577917554438_origin.png?io=w640 640w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-17921577917554438_origin.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-17921577917554438_origin.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-17921577917554438_origin.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"640\"/></a></span> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"> </p></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"regular-img-figure\" contenteditable=\"false\"><picture> <span><a aria-label=\"Expand image into lightbox view\" data-height=\"292\" data-og-image-facebook=\"false\" data-og-image-google_news=\"false\" data-og-image-google_plus=\"false\" data-og-image-linkedin=\"false\" data-og-image-msn=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_image_post=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_large_card=\"false\" data-og-image-twitter_small_card=\"false\" data-width=\"1144\" href=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-1792157791935417_origin.png\" rel=\"lightbox\" role=\"button\"><img alt=\"R2000\" contenteditable=\"false\" height=\"163\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 36px), (max-width: 1023px) calc(100vw - 180px), 552px\" src=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-1792157791935417_origin.png?io=w640\" srcset=\"https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-1792157791935417_origin.png?io=w640 640w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-1792157791935417_origin.png?io=w480 480w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-1792157791935417_origin.png?io=w320 320w,https://static.seekingalpha.com/uploads/2026/10/16/50624080-1792157791935417_origin.png?io=w240 240w\" width=\"640\"/></a></span> </picture><figcaption><p class=\"item-caption\"> </p></figcaption></figure></p> <p>Based on the chart above, current conditions place us squarely in the weakest cell of the top table: core inflation remains modestly above 2.5% (it was 2.6%) and rising as of the last CPI report for August. This is the one setting where small caps have historically done the worst.<sup><a href=\"https://riverwaterpartners.com/2026/10/15/small-caps-oil-first-fed-rate-hike-q3-2026/#footnote5\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">5</a></sup> We won’t pretend to know when the trend reversal will occur. History suggests it will eventually turn, and small-caps have posted their strongest median six-month returns when core inflation is below 2.5% and falling. We’d rather own the right businesses going into that shift than try to time it.</p> <p>We will continue to invest in companies that generate superior returns in their <a href=\"https://riverwaterpartners.com/asset-management/responsible-investing/\" rel=\"noopener\">responsibly deployed human, physical, and financial capital</a>. It is the discipline we have followed for a decade. As always, thank you for your trust and confidence. Please reach out with any questions.</p> <p><strong>Adam Peck</strong></p> <p>Co-Founder &amp; Chief Investment Officer, Riverwater Partners</p> <h3>Citations</h3> <p><sup>1</sup> [COMPLIANCE TO SUPPLY: Sustainable Value composite performance presentation and required disclosures supporting the since-inception, net-of-fees, standard deviation and beta comparison to the Russell 2500 Value Index.]</p> <p><sup>2</sup> Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, Federal Open Market Committee statement, September 16, 2026; target range for the federal funds rate raised 0.25 percentage point to 3.75%–4.00%. <a href=\"https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/fomccalendars.htm\" rel=\"noopener\">Meeting calendars and information</a></p> <p><sup>3</sup> Furey Research Partners; FactSet. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) crude oil, percentage change over the 12 months before the first rate hike of each Federal Reserve tightening cycle, 1983–84 through 2022–23. Today = September 14, 2026.</p> <p><sup>4</sup> Furey Research Partners; FactSet. Russell 2000 price return over the 12 months following the first hike of each of the seven prior Federal Reserve tightening cycles since 1983.</p> <p><sup>5</sup> U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, Consumer Price Index release for August 2026, published September 11, 2026. <a href=\"https://www.bls.gov/cpi/\" rel=\"noopener\">CPI Home</a>. Return data by inflation regime: Furey Research Partners and FactSet.</p> <div class=\"table-responsive\">\n<span class=\"sa-table-scroll-wrapper sa-hide-scrollbar\"><span data-intersection-boundary=\"start\" data-test-id=\"table-scroll-wrapper-boundary-start\"></span><table><tr><td> <p><em>The Russell 2000 Index measures the performance of the small-cap segment of the U.S. equity universe. The Russell 2500 Value Index measures the performance of the small- to mid-cap value segment of the U.S. equity universe. Indices are unmanaged and cannot be invested in directly.</em></p> <p><em>The information provided herein reflects the opinions of Riverwater Partners, LLC as of the date of publication and is subject to change without notice. It is provided for informational and educational purposes only and should not be construed as investment advice or a recommendation to buy or sell any security. Past performance is not indicative of future results. Investing involves risk, including the potential loss of principal. Indices cannot be invested in directly and are unmanaged. Riverwater Partners does not guarantee the accuracy or completeness of this information and is not responsible for any errors or omissions. Clients or prospective clients should consult their financial advisor before making any investment decisions. Riverwater Partners is a Registered Investment Advisor with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC).</em></p> </td></tr></table>\n<span data-intersection-boundary=\"end\" data-test-id=\"table-scroll-wrapper-boundary-end\"></span></span><button class=\"sa-table-enlarge-button\" type=\"button\">Click to enlarge</button>\n</div> <p><a href=\"https://riverwaterpartners.com/2026/10/15/small-caps-oil-first-fed-rate-hike-q3-2026/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"><em>Original Post</em></a></p> <p><strong>Editor's Note:</strong> The summary bullets for this article were chosen by Seeking Alpha editors.</p></body></html>",
